NNAAMMEE
       xtotroff - convert X font metrics into GNU troff font metrics

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       xxttoottrrooffff [--rr _r_e_s_o_l_u_t_i_o_n] [--ss _p_o_i_n_t_-_s_i_z_e] _f_o_n_t_-_m_a_p

       xxttoottrrooffff ----hheellpp

       xxttoottrrooffff --vv
       xxttoottrrooffff ----vveerrssiioonn

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       _x_t_o_t_r_o_f_f takes a _f_o_n_t_-_m_a_p, which maps _g_r_o_f_f(1) fonts to X11 fonts, cre‐
       ates GNU _t_r_o_f_f(1) metric files for all  fonts  listed.   Each  line  in
       _f_o_n_t_-_m_a_p  consists of a _g_r_o_f_f font name and an X font name as a X Logi‐
       cal Font Description (XLFD) pattern, separated by whitespace.  Example:

              TB -adobe-times-bold-r-normal--*-*-*-*-p-*-iso8859-1

       The wildcards in the patterns are filled with the arguments to  the  --rr
       and --ss switches.  If a font name is still ambiguous, _x_t_o_t_r_o_f_f aborts.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       Whitespace is permitted between a command-line option and its argument.

       ----hheellpp Display a usage message and exit.

       --rr_r_e_s_o_l_u_t_i_o_n
              Set the resolution for all font patterns in _f_o_n_t_-_m_a_p.  The value
              is used for both the horizontal and vertical resolution.  If not
              specified, a resolution of 75dpi is assumed.

       --ss_p_o_i_n_t_-_s_i_z_e
              Set  the  point  size for all font patterns in _f_o_n_t_-_m_a_p.  If not
              specified, a size of 10pt is assumed.

       --vv
       ----vveerrssiioonn
              Display version information and exit.

BBUUGGSS
       The only supported font encodings are “iso8859-1”  and  “adobe-fontspe‐
       cific”.

